# Lesson 3.3 example: records, field access, and collection tests

# Records keep named fields together.
invoice_one equals record with 1200 as amount and "pending" as status
invoice_two equals record with 300 as amount and "approved" as status

# Lists can contain records, not only plain text or numbers.
invoices equals list of invoice_one and invoice_two

# Current runtime helpers can sort and inspect the list.
sorted_invoices equals sort invoices
first_invoice equals first of sorted_invoices
last_invoice equals last of sorted_invoices

# Field access can be combined with first of and last of.
first_amount equals amount of first_invoice
last_status equals status of last_invoice

Print first_amount
Print last_status
